			   '"HPID allows the user to use the protein IDs in  ENSEMBL, HPRD and UniProt/Swiss-Prot ID to search protein interactions of interest."'
			   url:
			   'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query75').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Molecular Interaction'
			   name: 'ProNIT'
			   description:
			   '"ProNIT database provides experimentally determined thermodynamic interaction data between proteins and nucleic acids"'
			   url:
			   'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query76').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Molecular Interaction'
			   name: 'KDBI'
			   description:
			   '"Kinetic Data of Bio-molecular Interactions (KDBI) aimed at providing experimentally determined kinetic data of protein-protein, protein-RNA, protein-DNA, protein-ligand, RNA-ligand, DNA-ligand binding or reaction events described in the literature."'
			   url:
			   'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query78').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Molecular Interaction'
			   name: 'DDIB'
			   description:
			   '"The Database of Domain Interactions and Bindings (DDIB) collects information about domain-domain interactions and domain interactions with biological molecules such as nucleotides, peptides, inorganic ions, phospholipids."'
			   url:
			   'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query79').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Molecular Interaction'
			   name: 'IntAct project'
			   description:
			   '"IntAct provides a freely available, open source database system and analysis tools for molecular interaction data."'
			   url:
			   'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query80').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Molecular Interaction'
			   name: 'Epitome'
			   description:
			   '"Epitome is a database of all known antigenic residues and the antibodies that interact with them, including a detailed description of residues involved in the interaction and their sequence / structure environments."'
			   url: 'https://rostlab.org/services/epitome/') }
		  asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> mutationDatabases [
	"Secondary mutation databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'Imprinted Gene Catalogue' description: '"The database includes descriptions of 85 imprinted genes from several mammalian species, over 300 entries on reported parent-of-origin effects in animals, and 1700 mutations (found in 59 different genes) with a parent-of-origin effect. Data is accessed through a search engine and references are hyperlinked to PubMed, UCSC Genome Browser and Ensembl."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query68'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: '16Sand 23S rRNA Mutation Database' description: '"Expanded versions of the 16S and 23S Ribosomal RNA Mutation Databases"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query71'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'HGMD' description: '"The Human Gene Mutation Database (HGMD®) represents an attempt to collate known (published) gene lesions responsible for human inherited disease."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query74'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'BayGenomics' description: '"The BayGenomics gene-trap resource provides researchers with access to thousands of mouse embryonic stem (ES) cell lines harboring characterized insertional mutations in both known and novel genes."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query77'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'GeneTrap' description: '"Gene trapping is a high-throughput approach that is used to introduce insertional mutations across the genome in mouse embryonic stem (ES) cells. In addition to generating standard loss-of-function alleles, newer gene trap vectors offer a variety of post-insertional modification strategies for the generation of other experimental alleles. "' url: 'http://www.genetrap.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'Cypriot National mutation Database' description: '"Cypriot National Genetic Database is an online repository of information about inherited disorders in the Cypriot population."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query82'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'RBI Gene mutation database' description: '"RB1 Gene Mutation DB is a locus specific database that contains data on small mutations in RBI gene somatic and germline mutations."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query83'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Mutation' name: 'SSU rRNA modification database' description: '"The Small Subunit rRNA Modification Database provides a listing of reported post-transcriptionally modified nucleosides and sequence sites in small subunit rRNAs from bacteria, archaea and eukarya."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query85'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> nrspDatabases [
	"Primary nrsp databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'Links to AnGR Sites and DB resources' description: 'This site is maintained by National Animal Genome Research Program (NAGRP) (USDA NRSP-8 Livestock Genome Research Projects) and contains an extensive links to various websites and databases for livestock species' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/94'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NRSP-8 National Aquaculture Genome Projects' description: '"The National Aquaculture Genome Project is a part of the National Animal Genome Research Project. This site is designed to enhance collaboration, cooperation, communication, and coordination among aquaculture genome research community members."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/95'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NAGRM Genome Informatics Resources' description: 'This site of NAGRM contains links to Animal genome Data Resources (Map, EST, Bac Contig, HapMap) of several livestock species, Neighbourhood Links (Open Source Tools, DB Tools, Ontology, Fuctional genomics etc), NAGRP Tools resources etc.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/96'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NAGRP Tool Box' description: 'Useful Bioinformatics tools for molecular data analysis, viz. Beap, Categorizer, Cri-Map, SNPlotz etc.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/97'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NAGRP Blast Center' description: '"A number of BLAST options are available, namely, Regular BLAST, Mega BLAST, BLAST 2 sequences, mpiBLAST".' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/98'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NAGRP Cattle Genome Coordination Program' description: 'All required information (through links to main pages) regarding genomics and molecular genetics research on cattle, viz. Research Activities, Databases, Genome Maps, Resources etc. are available in one page.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/99'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NAGRP Cattle genome Maps' description: 'Cattle genome map & QTL maps from various resources are avilable, viz. Cattle Genome Map at NCBI (updated: 2003, 2007), Cattle Genome Map at USDA-MARC (1994, 1996, 2004), Bovine Genome Browser (TXAM Univ), The ArkDB - Cattle Map (Roslin Inst.), Texas A&M, Univ. of Sydney etc.' url: 'http://www.animalgenome.org/cattle/maps/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'AnGenMap' description: '"ANGENMAP (ANimal GENe MAPpers) is an internet discussion and information sharing group in the broad fields of animal genome research. The purpose of the group is to promote the exchange of information related but not limited to, animal gene mapping, genetics, genomics, and bioinformaitcs"' url: 'http://www.animalgenome.org/community/angenmap/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'Genome research Information Links' description: 'This wesite of NAGRP contains links to various useful areas of bioinformatics andbiological research, viz. Genome Databases, Literature Databases, Livestock Genomics Projects, Gene Prediction Software, Microarray Software and Databases, Genome Computing Resources, Journals in Biology, BioTech Companies and Patent and IP Resources' url: 'http://www.bioinfo-cbs.org/igd/description1.php2'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'AnimalQTLdb' description: 'QTL information on cattle, pig, sheep, horse, chicken, rainbow-trout are avilable. "The Animal Quantitative Trait Loci (QTL) database (Animal QTLdb) strives to collect all publicly available trait mapping data, i.e. QTL (phenotype/expression, eQTL), candidate gene and association data (GWAS) and copy number variations (CNV) mapped to livestock animal genomes, to facilitate locating and comparing discoveries within and between species. New data and database tools are continually developed to align various trait mapping data to map-based genome features, such as annotated genes".' url: 'http://www.animalgenome.org/cgi-bin/QTLdb/index'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'Ruminant Genome Biology Consortium' description: '"The Ruminant Genome Biology Consortium has been formed to capture the learning’s of communities who have already developed genomic tools for their own ruminant (Bovine. Ovine and Caprine) species"' url: 'http://www.animalgenome.org/ruminants/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'NAGRP Sheep / Small Ruminants Genome Coordination Program' description: 'All required information (through links to main pages) regarding genomics and molecular genetics research on sheep/small ruminants, viz. Research Activities, Databases, Genome Maps, Resources etc. are available in one page.' url: 'http://www.bioinfo-cbs.org/igd/description1.php5'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'Teleost Alternative Splicing Database' description: 'Alternative splicing information and related databases on catfish, zebrafish, fugu etc are available.' url: 'http://www.animalgenome.org/tasd'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'NRSP' name: 'Spidentifier v. Beta 1.10' description: '"This package is designed to predict the location of SNPs from clusters of ESTs produced by the program CAP3"' url: 'http://www.bioinfo-cbs.org/igd/description1.php7'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> nucleotideSequenceDatabases [
	"Primary nucleotide sequence databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'NCBI Home Page' description: 'It is a vast repository and a public database of nucleic acid sequences, literature and genome specific resources. Besides, it provides several biocomputational tools for sequence analysis and FTPs for sequence retreival. The various databases harbored by NCBI are "PubMed (biomedical literature citations and abstracts), PubMed Central (free, full text journal articles), Site Search (NCBI web and FTP sites), Books (online books), OMIM (online Mendelian Inheritance in Man ), Nucleotide (Core subset of nucleotide sequence records), EST (Expressed Sequence Tag records), GSS (Genome Survey Sequence records), Protein (sequence database), Genome (whole genome sequences), Structure (three-dimensional macromolecular structures), Taxonomy (organisms in GenBank), SNP (short genetic variations), dbVar (Genomic structural variation), Gene (gene-centered information), SRA (Sequence Read Archive), BioSystems (Pathways and systems of interacting molecules), HomoloGene (eukaryotic homology groups), Probe (sequence-specific reagents), BioProject (aggregated biological research project data ), dbGaP (genotype and phenotype), UniGene (gene-oriented clusters of transcript sequences), CDD (conserved protein domain database), Clone (integrated data for clone resources), UniSTS (markers and mapping data), PopSet (population study data sets), GEO Profiles (expression and molecular abundance profiles ), GEO DataSets (experimental sets of GEO data), Epigenomics (Epigenetic maps and data sets), PubChem BioAssay (bioactivity screens of chemical substances), PubChem Compound (unique small molecule chemical structures), PubChem Substance (deposited chemical substance records ), Protein Clusters (a collection of related protein sequences), OMIA (online Mendelian Inheritance in Animals), BioSample (biological material descriptions ), NLM Catalog (catalog of books, journals, and audiovisuals in the NLM collections) and MeSH (detailed information about NLM''s controlled vocabulary)".' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'NCBI-dbVar' description: 'dbVar is a database maintained by NCBI for "genomic structural variations".' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'GenBank' description: 'A public repository of nucleotide sequences provided by NCBI.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Genbank/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'NCBI Human Genome Browser' description: '"The NCBI Map Viewer provides graphical displays of features on the human reference genome sequence assembly maintained by the GRC and the alternate HuRef genome assembly, as well as cytogenetic, genetic, physical, and radiation hybrid maps. Map features can be seen along the sequence include genes, transcripts, NCBI contigs (the ''Contig'' map), the BAC tiling path (the ''Component'' map), STSs, FISH mapped clones, ESTs and transcripts from several different organisms, Gnomon predicted gene models" etc.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'NIH Human Microbiome Project' description: 'The Human Microbiome Project (HMP) is the initiative of United States National Institutes of Health "with the goal of identifying and characterizing the microorganisms which are found in association with both healthy and diseased humans".' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'Entrez' description: '"PubMed comprises more than 22 million citations for biomedical literature from MEDLINE, life science journals, and online books. Citations may include links to full-text content from PubMed Central and publisher web sites".' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?db=PubMed'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'NCBI GenBank Taxonomy Database' description: 'It provides taxonomical information of an organism (used in molecular biology research work).' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/taxonomyhome.html/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'EMBL-EBI' description: 'The EBI, a part of EMBL, is an academic research institute located on the Wellcome Trust Genome Campus in  Cambridge (UK). It serves as a public repository of molecular data. It also provides free online bioinformatic software and tools.' url: 'http://www.ebi.ac.uk'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'EMBL' description: '"The EMBL Nucleotide Sequence Database (also known as EMBL-Bank) constitutes Europe''s primary nucleotide sequence resource. Main sources for DNA and RNA sequences are direct submissions from individual researchers, genome sequencing projects and patent applications".' url: 'http://www.ebi.ac.uk/embl/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'DDBJ' description: '"The DNA Databank of Japan is one of the three summit databank that construct DDBJ/EMBL/GenBank International Nucleotide Sequence database through close collaboration of EBI in Europe and NCBI in USA".' url: 'http://www.ddbj.nig.ac.jp/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'Transcriptional Regulatory Element Database' description: 'This database is a good resource to obtain  training datasets for genome wide cis-regulatory element prediction, gene functional studies, and exploring gene regulatory networks' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/93'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'Promoter Analysis Pipeline (PAP)' description: 'It is used for analyzing set of coexpressed genes vis-a-vis predicting the transcriptional regulatory mechanisms' url: 'http://bioinformatics.wustl.edu/webTools/PromoterAnalysis.do'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'STACK' description: '"The STACKdb, Sequence Tag Alignment and Consensus Knowledgebase, is generated by processing EST and mRNA sequences obtained from GenBank through a pipeline consisting of masking, clustering, alignment and variation analysis steps"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/69'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'ENA Sequence Verion Archive' description: 'The ENA Sequence Version Archive is a repository of all entries which have ever appeared in EMBL-Bank Sequence Database.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/70'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'Clusters of orthologous groups of proteins (NCBI)' description: '"The COG protein database was generated by comparing predicted and known proteins in all completely sequenced microbial genomes to infer sets of orthologs. Each COG consists of a group of proteins found to be orthologous across at least three lineages and likely corresponds to an ancient conserved domain"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query86'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'Entrez Gene' description: '"Entrez Gene is NCBI''s repository for gene-specific information"' url: 'http://jura.wi.mit.edu/entrez_gene/'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'OMIA' description: '"Online Mendelian Inheritance in Animals (OMIA) is a catalogue/compendium of inherited disorders, other (single-locus) traits, and genes in 215 animal species (other than human and mouse and rats, which have their own resources)". "OMIA information is stored in a database that contains textual information and references, as well as links to relevant PubMed and Gene records at the NCBI, and to OMIM and Ensembl"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query88'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'Homophila' description: '"Homophila utilizes the sequence information of human disease genes from the NCBI OMIM (Online Mendelian Inheritance in Man) database in order to determine if sequence homologs of these genes exist in the current Drosophila sequence database (FlyBase). Sequences are compared using NCBI''s BLAST program. The database is updated weekly and can be searched by human disease, gene name, OMIM number, title, subtitle and/or allelic variant descriptions"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query89'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'PubChem' description: '"This database provides comprehensive search facilities for finding a particular component, or determining components in structure entries or vice versa."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query90'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'DDBJ Search and analysis tools' description: 'This is DDBJ page that contains several tols for Database search, Genome Analysis, NGS Analysis, Phylogenetics, Submission of gene expression data, Protein Dtatabase and structure etc.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query91'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'NCBI RefSeq' description: '"A comprehensive, integrated, non-redundant, well-annotated set of reference sequences including genomic, transcript, and protein"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query92'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'dbSNP' description: '"The Database of Short Genetic Variation (dbSNP)  is a public archive of all short sequence variation and includes a broad collection of simple genetic variations such as single-base nucleotide substitutions, small-scale multi-base deletions or insertions, and microsatellite repeats"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query93'.
		BioDatabase type: #primary category: 'Nucleotide Sequence' name: 'OMIM' description: 'It is an "Online Catalog of Human Genes and Genetic Disorders"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query94'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> otherStructuralDatabases [
	"Secondary other structural databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'ASD' description: '"Allosteric Database (ASD) provides a central resource for the display, search and analysis of the structure, function and related annotation for allosteric molecules."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query95'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'YDPM' description: '"The project aims to increase the understanding of mitochondrial function and biogenesis in the context of the cell."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query96'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'THGS' description: '"Transmembrane Helices in Genome Sequences (THGS v2) is an interactive web based database which has been developed to search the transmembrane helices in the user-defined genome available in the Genome Database (GDB)."' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query97'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'Structure superposition Database' description: '"The SSD has been developed to address the need for resources and tools for understanding large sets of superpositions in order to understand evolutionary relationships and to make predictions of function."' url: 'http://www.ssd.rbvi.ucsf.edu'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'MolMovDB' description: '"Database of Macromolecular Movements with Associated Tools for Flexibility and Geometric Analysis describes the motions that occur in proteins and other macromolecules"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mapview/map_search.cgi?chr=hum_chr.inf&query99'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'E-MSD' description: '"PDBe is the European resource for the collection, organisation and dissemination of data on biological macromolecular structures."' url: 'http://www.ebi.ac.uk/msd'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: '1MB Jena Image library' description: '"The Jena Library of Biological Macromolecules (JenaLib) is aimed at a better dissemination of information on three-dimensional biopolymer structures with an emphasis on visualization and analysis."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/01'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Structural' name: 'MMDB' description: '"The Molecular Modeling Database (MMDB) is a database of experimentally determined 3D-dimensional biomolecular structures and hosted by the National Center for Biotechnology Information"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Structure/MMDB/mmdb.shtml'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> otherUsefulDatabases [
	"Secondary other useful databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Useful' name: 'db resource of livestock' description: 'This website links to Animal Genomics Research Web Sites and Database Resources for almost all domestic animals and pets.' url: 'http://www.animalgenome.org/community/other.html'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Useful' name: 'Livestock Census 2007-India' description: 'Database of livestock census of India (2007).' url: 'http://dahd.nic.in/Default1.aspx'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Useful' name: 'Integrated Taxonomic Information System' description: 'To "find authoritative taxonomic information on plants, animals, fungi, and microbes of North America and the world".' url: 'http://www.itis.gov/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Useful' name: 'Multi-db' description: 'It links to various biological databases including, plant, animal and microbes. It also provides the links to search algorithms.' url: 'http://www.bcmsu.ac.in/BDBASE.HTM'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Useful' name: 'MySQL Website' description: 'For downloading of free as well as commercially available Enterprise version of MySQL.' url: 'http://www.mysql.com/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Other Useful' name: 'Supercomputing Facility for Bioinformatics & Computational Biology, IIT Delhi' description: 'A battery of useful bioinformatics software (drug designing, protein structure prediction etc.) are available in this link.' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbvar/04'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> parasiteDatabases [
	"Secondary parasite databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Parasite' name: 'Full-Malaria' description: '"FULL-malaria is a database for a full-length-enriched cDNA library from the human malaria parasite Plasmodium falciparum"' url: 'http://133.11.149.55/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Parasite' name: 'CandidaDB' description: '"A new multi-genome GenoList browser is available which includes the genomes of Candida albicans and other Candida species. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/04'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Parasite' name: 'TcruziDB' description: '"TcruziDB is an integrated genome database for the parasitic organism Trypanosoma cruzi, the causative agent of Chagas'' disease. "' url: 'http://www.tcruzidb.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Parasite' name: 'ToxoDB' description: '"ToxoDB is a genome and functional genomic database for the protozoan parasite Toxoplasma gondii. "' url: 'http://www.toxodb.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Parasite' name: 'PlasmoDB' description: '"PlasmoDB is a genomic database for the genus Plasmodium."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/07'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> phylogeneticDatabases [
	"Secondary phylogenetic databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'HOINVGEN release 01' description: '"HOINVGEN is a database of homologous invertebrate genes, structured under ACNUC sequence database management system. It allows one to select sets of homologous genes among invertebrate species, and to visualize multiple alignments and phylogenetic trees"' url: 'http://pbil.univ-lyon1.fr/databases/hoinvgen/HOINVGEN.html'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'Islander' description: '"Focuses on integrase phylogeny and helps understand how new site-specificity evolves, an important problem in genome evolution. Prokaryotic chromosomes often contain islands (prophages, pathogenicity islands, etc.) that were delivered by site-specific integrases. Most often the integration sites are in genes for tRNAs or other small RNAs."' url: 'http://cbs.ym.edu.tw/services/islander/islander.cgi'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'SRPDB' description: '"SRPDB (Signal Recognition Particle Database) provides aligned, annotated and phylogenetically ordered sequences related to structure and function of SRP. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/10'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'Tree of Life' description: '"The Tree of Life Web Project (ToL) is a collaborative effort of biologists and nature enthusiasts from around the world. "' url: 'http://tolweb.org/tree/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'TreeBase' description: '"TreeBASE is a repository of phylogenetic information, specifically user-submitted phylogenetic trees and the data used to generate them. TreeBASE accepts all types of phylogenetic data (e.g., trees of species, trees of populations, trees of genes) representing all biotic taxa"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/12'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'DART' description: '"The DART (Discovery and Aggregation of Relations in Text) database contains approximately 23 million distinct "world knowledge" propositions (110 million with duplicates), extracted from text by abstracting parse trees. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/13'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'PANDIT' description: '"Protein and Associated Nucleotide Domains with Inferred Trees"' url: 'http://www.ebi.ac.uk/goldman-srv/pandit'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'NeBI Taxonomy' description: '"The Taxonomy Database is a curated classification and nomenclature for all of the organisms in the public sequence databases"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/15'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'PALl' description: '"The database of Phylogeny and ALIgnment of homologous protein structures (PALI) contains structure-based sequence alignments and dendrograms based on information primarily derived from the structural alignments at domain level"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/16'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Phylogenetic' name: 'U-genome' description: '"This database is of importance in understanding unicellular genome design and architecture and evolution related studies."' url: 'http://www.sege.ntu.edu.sg/wester/ugenome/'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> plantBioinformaticsDatabases [
	"Secondary plant bioinformatics databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PLACE' description: '"PLACE is a database of motifs found in plant cis-acting regulatory DNA elements, all from previously published reports."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/18'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PlantCARE' description: '"PlantCARE is a database of plant cis-acting regulatory elements, enhancers and repressors."' url: 'www.bioinformatics.psb.ugent.be/webtools/plantcare/html/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'AGRIS' description: '"AGRIS (International System for Agricultural Science and Technology) is a global public domain database with more than 4 million structured bibliographical records on agricultural science and technology."' url: 'http://agris.fao.org/agris-search/index.do'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'ARAMEMNON' description: '"A specialized database (DB) for Arabidopsis membrane proteins, ARAMEMNON, was designed that facilitates the interpretation of gene and protein sequence data by integrating features that are presently only available from individual sources."' url: 'http://aramemnon.uni-koeln.de/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Arabidopsis Nucleolar' description: '"The Arabidopsis Nucleolar Protein Database provides information on 217 proteins identified in a proteomic analysis of nucleoli isolated from Arabidopsis cell culture. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/22'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'SGMD' description: '"It serves both as a sequence repository, holding DNA sequences for numerous EST''s, and also as a microarray experiment database. It allows scientists to explore the expression levels of the EST clones stored in the database and to correlate expression levels with function."' url: 'http://bioinformatics.towson.edu/SGMD/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Rice PIPELINE' description: '"The Rice PIPELINE is a unification tool for plant functional genomics."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/24'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'DATF' description: '"The Database of Arabidopsis Transcription Factors (DATF) collects all arabidopsis transcription factors (totally 1922 Loci; 2290 Gene Models) and classifies them into 64 families."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/25'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'GabiPD' description: '"GabiPD constitutes a repository and analysis platform for a wide array of heterogeneous data from high-throughput experiments in several plant species. "' url: 'http://gabi.rzpd.de/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PoMaMo' description: '"This is the database for potato maps and more"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/27'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Rice Proteome Database' description: '"The information thus obtained from the rice proteome will be helpful in predicting the function of the unknown proteins and aid in their molecular cloning."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/28'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Brassica ASTRA' description: '"Brassica ASTRA is a public database for genomic information on Brassica species. The database incorporates expressed sequences with Swiss-Prot and GenBank comparative sequence annotation as well as secondary Gene Ontology (GO) annotation derived from the comparison with Arabidopsis TAIR GO annotations."' url: 'http://hornbill.cspp.latrobe.edu.au'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PlantProm' description: '"PlantProm DB, a plant promoter database, is an annotated, non-redundant collection of proximal promoter sequences for RNA polymerase II with experimentally determined transcription start site(s), TSS, from various plant species."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/30'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'TIGR Maize Database' description: '"TIGR maize database"' url: 'http://maize.jcvi.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'MOsDB' description: '"The MOsDB is a resource for publicly available sequences of the rice (Oryza sativa L.) genome"' url: 'http://mips.helmholtz-muenchen.de/plant/rice/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'ARTADEdb' description: '"ARTADE (ARabidopsis Tiling-Array-based Detection of Exons) is a standard tool for the annotation of genome-wide tiling-array data in Arabidopsis."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/33'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'OryGenesDB' description: '"The aim of this Oryza sativa database is to display sequence information resulting from the activities of our group, such as the T-DNA and Ds flanking sequence tags (FSTs) produced in the framework of the French genomics initiative Genoplante and the EU consortium Cereal Gene Tags. "' url: 'http://orygenesdb.cirad.fr/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Oryza Tag Line Data-' description: '"Oryza Tag Line consists in a searchable database integrating phenotypic data resulting from the evaluation of the G' url: 'http://oryzatagline.cirad.fr/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PLANT-PIs' description: '"PlantPIs is a web querying system for a database collecting plant protease inhibitors data"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/36'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PlantsP/PlantsT' description: '"The PLANTS Database provides standardized information about the vascular plants, mosses, liverworts, hornworts, and lichens of the U.S. and its territories."' url: 'http://plants.usda.gov/java/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'RARGE' description: '" To enhance the utility of the RIKEN Arabidopsis resource (full-length cDNAs, transposon mutants and microarray experiments),  RARGE database was constructed. In order to facilitate effectively phenomics studies,  the area of data was integrated from genome to phenome such as Ds tagged mutant and nuclear-encoded chloroplast proteins."' url: 'http://rarge.psc.riken.jp/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'BGI-RISe' description: '"In BGI-RIS, sequence contigs of Beijing indica and Syngenta japonica have been further assembled and anchored onto the rice chromosomes. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/39'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'RiceGAAS' description: '"RiceGAAS is a rice genome automated annotation system. This system integrates programs for prediction and analysis of protein-coding gene structure."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/40'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'RMD' description: '"Rice Mutant Database (RMD) is an archive for collecting, managing and searching information of the T-DNA insertion mutants generated by an enhancer trap system."' url: 'http://rmd.ncpgr.cn/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'TropGENE DB' description: '"TropGeneDB is a database that manages genomic, genetic and phenotypic information about tropical crops. It is organised on a crop basis."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/42'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'GrainGenes' description: '"Graingenes is the international database for the wheat, barley, rye and oat genomes. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/43'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'SoyGD' description: '"The Soybean GBrowse Database combines Perl MySQL database programming with Gbrowse to provide an integrated way of presenting soybean genomic features. "' url: 'http://www.soybeangenome.siu.edu'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'TAIR' description: '"The Arabidopsis Information Resource (TAIR) maintains a database of genetic and molecular biology data for the model higher plant Arabidopsis thaliana "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/45'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'AthaMap' description: '"AthaMap provides a genome-wide map of potential transcription factor and small RNA binding sites in Arabidopsis thaliana."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/46'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'CATMA' description: '"The aim of the Complete Arabidopsis Transcriptome MicroArray (CATMA) project was the design and production of high quality Gene-specific Sequence Tags (GSTs) covering most Arabidopsis genes"' url: 'http://www.catma.org'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Lis (formerly MGI)' description: '"The mission of LIS is to enable productive applied and basic research in the legumes by relating data from multiple crop and model species, and by helping researchers traverse among various data types."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/48'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'base' description: '"RAD is a contig-oriented database for high-quality manual annotation of RGP, which can present non-redundant contig analyses by merging the accumulated PAC/BAC clones."' url: 'http://www.golgi.gs.dna.affrc.gojp/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Gramene' description: '"Gramene is a curated, open-source, integrated data resource for comparative functional genomics in crops and model plant species."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/50'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'IRIS' description: 'The International Rice Information System "is the rice implementation of the International Crop Information System (ICIS) which is a database system that provides integrated management of global information on genetic resources and crop cultivars"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/51'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'MaizeGDB' description: '"MaizeGDB is the community database for biological information about the crop plant Zea mays."' url: 'http://www.maizegdb.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PlantMarkers' description: '"PlantMarkers is a genetic marker database that contains a comprehensive pool of predicted molecular markers."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/53'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'MAtDB' description: '"The MAtDB aims to provide a comprehensive resource for Arabidopsis as a genome model that serves as a primary reference for research in plants and is suitable for transfer of knowledge to other plants, especially crops."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/54'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Panzea' description: '" "The Panzea Database contains the genotypic and phenotypic data and genetic marker information produced by the NSF-funded project ''Genetic Architecture of Maize and Teosinte''. "' url: 'http://www.panzea.org/database/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PlantGDB' description: '"PlantGDB is a database of molecular sequence data for all plant species with significant sequencing efforts"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/56'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'RAP-DB' description: 'The Rice Annotation Project (RAP) database.' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/57'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Seed Genes' description: '"This project deals with genes that exhibit a seed phenotype when disrupted by a loss-of-function mutation"' url: 'http://www.seedgenes.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'Oryzabase' description: '"The Oryzabase is a comprehensive rice science database established in 2000 by rice researcher''s committee in Japan. The database is originally aimed to gather as much knowledge as possible ranging from classical rice genetics to recent genomics and from fundamental information to hot topics"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/59'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'TED' description: '"Tomato functional genomics database"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/60'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'WAtDB' description: '"wageningen arabidopsis thaliana database (watdb) is a new, web-accessible database with curated data on Arabidopsis thaliana mutants."' url: 'http://www.watdb.nl'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'AGNS' description: '"AGNS (Arabidopsis GeneNet supplementary) database is an Internet-available resource that provides access to description of the functions of the known Arabidopsis genes at various levels-the levels of mRNA, protein, cell, tissue, and ultimately at the levels of organs and the organism in both wild type and mutant backgrounds."' url: 'http://wwwmgs.bionet.nsc.ru/agns/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'PhytoProt' description: '"The general procedure behind PHYTOPROT consists in performing an "all-by-all" comparison of (putative) protein sequences with the BIOFACET software, building clusters of sequences (Mohseni-Zadeh et al., Recomb 2003) based on their similarity and finally displaying' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/63'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Plant Bioinformatics' name: 'TIGR plant repeat database' description: '"The TIGR plant repeat database is a repository of repetitive sequences in plants."' url: 'https://plantrepeats.plantbiology.msu.edu/?'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> prokaryoticDatabases [
	"Secondary prokaryotic databases."
	^ {
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'DEG Database' description: 'It is a Database of essential genes from bacteria and yeast' url: 'http://tubic.tju.edu.cn/deg/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'EcoGene' description: '"EcoGene.org is a genome database and website dedicated to Escherichia coli K-12 substrain MG1655 that is revised daily using information derived from the biomedical literature and in-house analysis."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/66'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'LeptoList' description: '"A complete dataset of DNA and protein sequences derived from the paradigm strain L. interrogans serovar Lai, linked to the relevant annotations and functional assignments"' url: 'http://bioinfo.hku.hk/LeptoList'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'DOOR' description: 'It’s a "Complete and reliable operon database covering 2072 bacteria genomes and with overall accuracy of ~90% "' url: 'http://csbl.bmb.uga.edu/DOOR/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'PSORTdb' description: '"PSORTdb (part of the PSORT family) is a database of protein subcellular localizations for bacteria and archaea that contains both information determined through laboratory experimentation (ePSORTdb dataset) and computational predictions (cPSORTdb dataset)."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/69'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'Genolist' description: '"GenoList: an integrated environment for comparative analysis of microbial genomes"' url: 'http://genodb.pasteur.fr/cgi-bin/WebObjects/GenoList'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'CyanoBase' description: '"CyanoBase is the genome database for cyanobacteria, which are model organisms for photosynthesis. The database houses cyanobacteria species information, complete genome sequences, genome-scale experiment data, gene information, gene annotations and mutant information."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/71'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'GenProtEC' description: '"GenProtEC website was dedicated to the functions encoded by the Escherichia coli K-12 (strain MG1655) "' url: 'http://genprotec.mbl.edu/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'IMG' description: '"The mission of the Integrated Microbial Genomes (IMG) system is to support the annotation, analysis and distribution of microbial genome and metagenome datasets sequenced at DOE''s Joint Genome Institute (JGI). IMG is also open to scientists worldwide for the annotation, analysis, and distribution of their own genome and metagenome datasets, as long as they agree with the IMG data release policy and follow the metadata requirements for integrating data into IMG "' url: 'http://img.jgi.doe.gov/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'MBGD' description: '"MBGD is a database for comparative analysis of completely sequenced microbial genomes, the number of which is now growing rapidly. The aim of MBGD is to facilitate comparative genomics from various points of view such as ortholog identification, paralog clustering, motif analysis and gene order comparison"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/74'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'OPERON' description: 'It’s a site that allows us to "to detect and analyze conserved gene pairs - pairs of genes that are located close on the same DNA strand in two or more bacterial genomes. For each conserved gene pair", the algorithm "calculate an estimate of probability that the genes belong to the same operon"' url: 'http://operondb.cbcb.umd.edu/cgi-bin/operondb/operons.cgi'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'VirFact' description: '"Bacterial virulence factors and pathogenicity islands"' url: 'http://www.virfact.burnham.org'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'EcoCyc' description: '"EcoCyc is a scientific database for the bacterium Escherichia coli K-12 MG1655. The EcoCyc project performs literature-based curation of the entire genome, and of transcriptional regulation, transporters, and metabolic pathways"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/77'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'BSD' description: '"The Biodegradative Strain Database (BSD) is a freely-accessible, web-based database providing detailed information on degradative bacteria and the hazardous substances that they degrade, including corresponding literature citations, relevant patents and links to additional web-based biological and chemical data"' url: 'http://www.bsd.cme.msu.edu/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'ClostriDB' description: '"A database for Clostridium genome analysis."' url: 'http://www.clostri.bham.ac. uk/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'GenoBase' description: '"Public repository for Sequence Information, Proteome, Transcriptome, Bioinformatics, and Knowledge based on literature concerning E. coli."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/80'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'EHCO' description: '"EchoBASE is a relational database designed to contain and manipulate information from post-genomic experiments using the model bacterium Escherichia coli K-12. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/81'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'EchoBASE' description: '"EchoBASE is a relational database designed to contain and manipulate information from post-genomic experiments using the model bacterium Escherichia coli K-12."' url: 'http://www.ecoli-york.org/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'Extra-TRAIN' description: '"ExtraTrain is a database for exploring Extragenic space and Transcriptional information in bacteria and archaea."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/83'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'GeneDB' description: '"The GeneDB project is a core part of the Sanger Institute''s Pathogen Genomics activities. Its primary goals are: to provide reliable access to the latest sequence data and annotation/curation for the whole range of  organisms sequenced by the Pathogen group and to develop the website and other tools to aid the community in accessing and obtaining the maximum value from these data.' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/84'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'Colibri' description: '"This server is constructed around a database dedicated to the analysis of the genome of Escherichia coli: Colibri.Its purpose is to collate and integrate various aspects of the genomic information from E. coli, the paradigm of Gram-negative bacteria."' url: 'http://www.genolist.pasteur.fr/Colibri'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'Essential Genes in E.coli' description: '"It provides links to data on essential genes in E. coli, and shows a short list of E. coli essential genes identified from the Neidhardt E. coli books "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/86'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'E. coli ASAP' description: '"ASAP is a relational database and web interface developed to store, update, and distribute genome sequences in conjunction with associated annotations and functional characterization data"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/87'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'UM-BBD' description: '"UM-BBD allows to Search for curated information on microbial catabolism and related biotransformations, primarily for environmental pollutants."' url: 'http://www.hsls.pitt.edu/obrc/index.php?page=URL1100188151'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'EMGlib' description: '"The Enhanced Microbial Genomes Library (EMGLib) is a database system containing all the complete genomes sequenced from prokaryotic organisms (bacteria and archaea)"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/89'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'MetaGrowth' description: '"Metagrowth is a database aiming to guide experimental studies and in silico simulation studies on the culture conditions of obligate parasitic bacteria. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/90'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'CIDB' description: '"The Chlamydia Interactive Database (CIDB) described here is the first database of its type that holds genomic, RT-PCR, microarray and proteomics data sets that can be cross-queried by researchers for patterns in the data."' url: 'http://www.it.deakin.edu.au/CIDB'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'TIGR Microbial Database' description: '"The Comprehensive Microbial Resource (CMR) is a free tool that allows researchers to access all of the publicly available bacterial genome sequences completed to date"' url: 'http://www.jcvi.org/cms/research/past-projects/cmr/overview/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'PromEC' description: '"PromEC is an updated compilation of E. coli mRNA promoter sequences. It includes documentation on the location of experimentally identified mRNA transcriptional start sites on the E. coli chromosome, as well as the actual sequences in the promoter region. "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/93'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'MeGX' description: '"Megx.net allows access to integrated environmental and (meta)genomic data intended for use in marine microbial ecology"' url: 'http://www.Megx.net'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'PGTdb' description: '"PGTdb integrates microorganisms'' growth temperature data from literature survey with their nucleotide/protein sequence, protein family and structure data from related databases."' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/95'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'VBI Microbial Database' description: '"The VBI Microbial Database hosts data from different sources for a range of plant pathogenic oomycetes, fungi and bacteria, primarily those organisms under study at VBI"' url: 'http://www.phytophthora.vbi.vt.edu'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'CyberCell database' description: '"The CyberCell database (CCDB) is a comprehensive collection of detailed enzymatic, biological, chemical, genetic, and molecular biological data about E. coli "' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/97'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: '~CTOR db' description: '"Tractor_DB (v.2.0) contains a collection of computationally predicted Transcription Factors'' binding sites in gamma-proteobacterial genomes"' url: 'http://www.hmpdacc.org/resources/data_browser.php/98'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'CampyDB' description: '"CampyDB is a database for Campylobacter genome analysis. It allows users to conduct search, blast, sequence pattern search and genome browsing."' url: 'http://www.xbase.ac.uk/campydb/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'coliBase' description: '"xBASE2: a comprehensive resource for comparative bacterial genomics. It is a is a genome database aimed at helping laboratory-based bacteriologists make best use of bacterial genome sequence data, with a particular emphasis on comparative genomics."' url: 'http://www.xbase.ac.uk/colibase/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'ISfinder' description: '"IS finder database provides a list of insertion sequences isolated from eubacteria and archae. It is organised into individual files containing their general features (name, size, origin, family.....) as well as their DNA and potential protein sequences."' url: 'https://www-is.biotoul.fr/'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'RegulonDB' description: '"RegulonDB is a database of the regulatory network of Escherichia coli K-12"' url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?db=PubMed02'.
		BioDatabase type: #secondary category: 'Prokaryotic' name: 'Virulence Factors' description: '"a reference database for bacterial virulence factors."' url: 'www.mgc.ac.cn/VFs/?'.
	} asOrderedCollection
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
BioDatabases class >> promoterAndTranscriptionFactorDatabases [
	"Secondary promoter & transcription factor databases."

	^ {
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'ABS DB'
			   description:
			   'It is "a database of Annotated regulatory Binding Sites from orthologous promoters"'
			   url: 'http://genome.crg.es/datasets/abs2005/').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'TRED'
			   description:
			   '"TRED is a resource for studies on gene function and regulation. It provides cis-elements, such as promoters and binding motifs, and trans-elements, such as transcriptional factors (TFs)."'
			   url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?db=PubMed05').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'DPInteract'
			   description:
			   '"DPInteract: A database on DNA-protein interactions."'
			   url: 'http://arep.med.harvard.edu/dpinteract/').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'JASPAR'
			   description:
			   '"The JASPAR CORE database contains a curated, non-redundant set of profiles, derived from published collections of experimentally defined transcription factor binding sites for eukaryotes."'
			   url: 'http://jaspar.binf.ku.dk/').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'MPromDB'
			   description:
			   '"MPromDb (Mammalian Promoter Database) is a curated database that strives to annotate gene promoters identified from ChIP-Seq experiment results. "'
			   url: 'http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?db=PubMed08').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'DBTBS'
			   description:
			   '"DBTBS is a database of transcriptional regulation in Bacillus subtilis containing upstream intergenic conservation information. "'
			   url: 'http://www.dbtbs.hgc.jp/').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'DoOP'
			   description:
			   '"DoOP is a database of eukaryotic promoter sequences (upstream regions), aiming to facilitate the recognition of regulatory sites conserved between species."'
			   url: 'http://www.doop.abc.hu/').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
			   name: 'EPD'
			   description:
			   '"The Eukaryotic Promoter Database is an annotated non-redundant collection of eukaryotic POL II promoters, for which the transcription start site has been determined experimentally."'
			   url: 'http://www.epd.isb-sib.ch').
		  (BioDatabase
			   type: #secondary
			   category: 'Promoter & Transcription Factor'
